WEBVTT

00:00.317 --> 00:04.151
Episode 7
Cyber

00:21.372 --> 00:22.361
One.

00:22.473 --> 00:23.940
Zero.

00:24.041 --> 00:28.478
A world that can show every incident
using just zero and one.

00:29.547 --> 00:33.608
A realm that can never be reached
by human consciousness.

00:33.717 --> 00:38.586
A simple, undecorated space
that's possible only by computers.

00:39.723 --> 00:40.621
And...

00:41.792 --> 00:44.090
...the world that I love most.

01:15.459 --> 01:17.256
You're up rather early.

01:18.395 --> 01:20.863
I couldn't help but wake up early.

01:20.965 --> 01:22.364
Could it be my age?

01:23.500 --> 01:24.831
Impossible.

01:24.935 --> 01:26.300
Would you like some tea?

01:26.403 --> 01:27.665
Sure.

01:27.771 --> 01:30.365
I haven't seen Satsuki
since yesterday.

01:30.474 --> 01:32.908
She's been with her lover
all this time.

01:33.010 --> 01:37.276
You mean her lover in that
ominously cold refrigerator room?

01:38.749 --> 01:39.807
Yes.

01:39.917 --> 01:42.147
Satsuki is loved by him.

01:42.253 --> 01:43.584
Are you jealous?

01:43.687 --> 01:45.655
Yes, a little bit.

01:45.756 --> 01:48.088
A girl loved by a computer...

01:48.192 --> 01:50.820
there's nobody like her
anywhere else.

01:50.928 --> 01:55.024
There was a regional
blackout in Tokyo once.

01:55.132 --> 01:57.430
The one where all bank data
disappeared,

01:57.534 --> 02:00.833
and all telephone companies
lost communication.

02:00.938 --> 02:02.235
Could that be...

02:03.407 --> 02:04.704
Yes.

02:04.808 --> 02:06.833
I asked for Imperial
Household Office,

02:06.944 --> 02:08.741
and Cabinet Information
Research Office data.

02:09.313 --> 02:10.837
After hacking in...

02:10.948 --> 02:15.510
...she turned every power switch off
to escape tracing programs.

02:15.619 --> 02:18.747
For such a cute face,
she does rather extravagant things.

02:18.856 --> 02:21.916
That's why everyone wanted her.

02:23.394 --> 02:25.362
You're one of them, right?

02:29.300 --> 02:32.167
I always get what I want
at any cost.

02:38.175 --> 02:40.473
I wonder if
she gets jealous, too.

02:41.578 --> 02:45.241
Is that why you purposely
left the door ajar?

02:45.349 --> 02:46.373
Who knows?

03:24.088 --> 03:25.749
That feels good!

03:25.856 --> 03:29.348
Hey, Inuki, it's a good thing
we came to Tokyo.

03:29.460 --> 03:32.190
We met a lot of people
that can see you...

03:32.296 --> 03:34.457
...so you're not
lonely anymore, right?

03:40.871 --> 03:41.929
Good morning.

03:43.040 --> 03:44.166
Good morning.

03:44.274 --> 03:46.765
U-Um, are you on a walk?

03:46.877 --> 03:50.108
Yes, just for a change of pace.

03:50.214 --> 03:51.772
Do you come here often?

03:53.484 --> 03:54.542
Once in a while.

04:01.225 --> 04:03.989
The people in that car
are looking over here.

04:06.530 --> 04:08.020
You have good eyesight.

04:08.132 --> 04:09.565
Why are they looking this way?

04:09.666 --> 04:11.497
Are they people you know?

04:11.602 --> 04:12.660
You could say that.

04:15.038 --> 04:16.369
Have some if you'd like.

04:16.473 --> 04:18.134
T-Thank you.

04:18.242 --> 04:20.073
Don't worry.

04:20.177 --> 04:22.441
This has nothing to do with you.

04:26.650 --> 04:28.618
You can see Inuki?

04:30.854 --> 04:31.912
U-Um...

04:33.857 --> 04:34.915
What about this?

05:00.484 --> 05:02.179
They're a persistent bunch.

05:02.286 --> 05:04.186
Picking up where
they left off before?

05:53.904 --> 05:56.998
Why are humans so annoying?

05:58.742 --> 06:00.972
I just want to be free.

06:06.316 --> 06:08.045
Who is it?

06:08.151 --> 06:09.118
Who's there?

06:17.961 --> 06:19.485
Is someone there?

06:27.971 --> 06:29.268
Yeah.

06:29.373 --> 06:31.102
I'm Satsuki.

06:34.111 --> 06:35.476
I can't!

06:35.579 --> 06:38.309
This is what
father uses for work.

06:38.415 --> 06:40.781
He always tells me
never to touch it.

06:44.488 --> 06:46.786
My future?

06:46.890 --> 06:48.790
How do you know that?

06:51.028 --> 06:53.326
Yeah, I want to ask...

06:54.698 --> 06:56.598
Is it really all right?

07:12.282 --> 07:13.442
So beautiful!

07:15.052 --> 07:16.952
This is a wonderful place!

07:34.571 --> 07:36.300
S-Satsuki.

07:37.474 --> 07:38.634
Satsuki.

07:42.546 --> 07:44.138
What an amazing feat...

07:44.247 --> 07:47.216
going through all these guard
programs instantly.

07:47.317 --> 07:50.411
It's as if her brain
was connected to the computer.

07:50.520 --> 07:54.217
Please, allow us to take
your daughter under our care.

07:54.324 --> 07:58.283
Well, there are many people
who would say that.

07:58.395 --> 08:02.297
But my daughter is still
in grade school.

08:02.399 --> 08:03.297
However...

08:03.400 --> 08:06.392
Well,
this is enough for now.

08:06.503 --> 08:08.664
We'll talk in detail
another day.

08:08.772 --> 08:10.330
Yes, let's.

08:12.476 --> 08:13.500
How was it?

08:13.610 --> 08:14.474
Was it fun?

08:15.879 --> 08:18.609
I want to go home now.

08:20.851 --> 08:24.218
I'll be late tonight,
so I won't need dinner.

08:24.321 --> 08:25.879
Yes, I understand.

08:26.990 --> 08:28.150
Satsuki.

08:28.258 --> 08:33.662
You still might not understand,
but you have a wonderful talent.

08:33.764 --> 08:37.666
That laboratory is going to help
make full use of it.

08:37.768 --> 08:40.100
It might be tough
in the beginning,

08:40.203 --> 08:42.569
but it'll be fun
as you get used to it.

08:42.673 --> 08:44.538
You will go for me, Satsuki?

08:45.676 --> 08:47.166
I don't want to go.

08:47.277 --> 08:48.801
It's for your own good.

08:49.913 --> 08:52.040
I don't like it there.

08:52.149 --> 08:53.810
I love computers,

08:53.917 --> 08:56.078
but I hate those people.

08:56.186 --> 08:58.120
I want to be by myself.

08:58.221 --> 08:59.483
You can't.

08:59.589 --> 09:02.990
I thought about your future
and decided on this.

09:03.093 --> 09:05.061
The lab people
will come tomorrow.

09:05.162 --> 09:07.062
Don't be so selfish and go.

09:08.498 --> 09:09.931
Why?

09:10.033 --> 09:13.298
Why do you get to decide
my future, Father?

09:13.403 --> 09:15.928
Because you are
my precious daughter.

09:16.039 --> 09:18.371
It's because I love you.

09:18.475 --> 09:20.272
You understand, Satsuki?

09:22.079 --> 09:24.240
I don't want to go anywhere.

09:24.347 --> 09:26.338
That's such a boring place...

09:26.450 --> 09:30.011
...where all they do
is force boring games on me.

09:30.120 --> 09:33.715
I just want to talk to all of you.

09:35.125 --> 09:36.854
I hate father.

09:36.960 --> 09:40.157
I wish father
was no longer here.

09:40.263 --> 09:42.026
Please, help me.

09:43.100 --> 09:44.328
Help me!

09:49.306 --> 09:52.469
Yes, please give my daughter
the best care.

09:52.576 --> 09:54.669
Then I'll be waiting tomorrow.

10:36.753 --> 10:38.550
Miss Yatouji is amazing!

10:38.655 --> 10:40.714
Yeah, great!
I so look up to her!

10:46.396 --> 10:47.363
Impossible.

10:47.464 --> 10:52.902
To return it you need to increase
muscle power in your triceps by 13%,

10:53.003 --> 10:56.871
and in your hamstrings
by about 21%.

11:01.344 --> 11:02.936
- She did it!
- Wonderful!

11:03.046 --> 11:04.843
Miss Yatouji!

11:04.948 --> 11:06.506
It's such a simple thing.

11:07.617 --> 11:09.949
It's not even a game
when I'm facing humans.

11:10.053 --> 11:11.782
Please.

11:11.888 --> 11:13.822
Humans are so pitiful.

11:13.924 --> 11:15.892
They don't have
the ability to learn.

11:15.992 --> 11:19.587
Repeating the same mistakes
and not changing in the end.

11:19.696 --> 11:22.062
They waste away
each day just living.

11:23.166 --> 11:25.999
As if they were a program
in an infinite loop.

11:33.443 --> 11:35.741
We're here to pick you up.

11:35.846 --> 11:39.338
I heard your father passed away
in an accident the other day.

11:39.449 --> 11:41.713
I'm truly sorry to hear it.

11:41.818 --> 11:42.842
Well?

11:42.953 --> 11:45.353
Can you come
to our laboratory?

11:46.556 --> 11:51.016
Or would it be all right to tell
the police about what we know?

11:52.829 --> 11:55.389
That it wasn't
an accident at all.

12:05.809 --> 12:06.867
Initiate.

12:08.345 --> 12:10.006
Yesod.

12:10.113 --> 12:11.774
Netzach.

12:11.882 --> 12:13.406
Hod.

12:13.516 --> 12:15.040
Geburah.

12:15.151 --> 12:16.516
Chesed.

12:16.620 --> 12:18.178
- Thiphareth.
- She's perfect.

12:18.288 --> 12:19.186
Binah.

12:19.289 --> 12:20.881
It's only been a few months.

12:20.991 --> 12:24.620
To think she understands Sephiroth
to this level at age 14.

12:24.728 --> 12:25.752
Chokmah.

12:25.862 --> 12:27.989
- Kether.
- As long as we have her power...

12:28.098 --> 12:30.760
...we can control
the world at will!

12:32.802 --> 12:36.863
Satsuki, stay put there until
we move to the next stage.

12:36.973 --> 12:40.033
Stay put there until we move
to the next stage.

12:40.143 --> 12:41.508
This is boring.

12:41.611 --> 12:43.135
Humans are really boring.

12:44.247 --> 12:47.216
And the people obsessed
with me are the worst.

12:48.318 --> 12:50.548
I'm bored of
spending every day here.

12:51.655 --> 12:56.058
The only time I have fun
is when I'm talking with you guys.

12:56.159 --> 12:59.754
You told me that I'm
one of the Seven Angels,

12:59.863 --> 13:02.525
and that I'll fight
the Seven Seals.

13:03.600 --> 13:06.262
And soon... he will appear.

13:06.369 --> 13:08.428
The one who holds
the key to this world.

13:09.539 --> 13:11.564
That is "Kamui."

13:13.243 --> 13:16.110
I wonder if "Kamui"
is like Ain Soph?

13:17.347 --> 13:20.373
A realm beyond the limits
of human consciousness.

13:20.483 --> 13:23.077
An absolute power
surpassing even God.

13:23.186 --> 13:26.019
Though that may
as well be you guys.

13:27.090 --> 13:30.321
Will "Kamui" amuse me
at least a little bit?

13:32.595 --> 13:34.859
Satsuki, we're starting
the next test.

13:36.366 --> 13:39.358
Hey, how about
getting out of here soon?

13:47.177 --> 13:49.042
Hey, what's going on?

13:49.145 --> 13:50.043
Hey!

14:20.477 --> 14:21.375
Shit!

14:37.660 --> 14:39.457
Don't worry.

14:39.562 --> 14:41.257
It's not that I'm after you.

14:43.366 --> 14:44.924
I am Kanoe.

14:45.035 --> 14:49.199
One connected to the Final Battle,
just like you.

14:49.305 --> 14:52.570
I've been looking for you,
one of the Seven Angels.

14:53.643 --> 14:55.372
Come with me if you'd like.

14:55.478 --> 14:57.571
I have something to show you.

15:17.033 --> 15:19.024
I prepared this just for you.

15:20.136 --> 15:22.297
Doesn't it look like a fun friend?

15:24.140 --> 15:26.438
I'm sure you
won't be bored by him.

15:28.411 --> 15:30.971
That's how I got to meet Kanoe.

15:32.282 --> 15:36.912
She was different from
those who surrounded my life.

15:37.020 --> 15:37.987
And...

15:38.088 --> 15:41.216
...a free world, where it was
only me, was there.

16:06.349 --> 16:08.613
Long time no see.

16:08.718 --> 16:10.879
We've been looking
for you for a while.

16:10.987 --> 16:15.083
Now, I'll have you
quietly return under us.

16:15.191 --> 16:17.056
I hate to say this,
but I decline.

16:18.595 --> 16:20.426
Don't get me wrong.

16:20.530 --> 16:22.464
You have no right to choose.

16:28.071 --> 16:29.698
W-What the hell's this about?

16:40.383 --> 16:43.409
If the power goes on,
we'll all be electrocuted.

16:45.288 --> 16:47.916
Do you plan to die
and take us with you?

16:48.992 --> 16:50.687
Go ahead and try.

16:50.793 --> 16:55.093
Does a little girl like you
know what it means to die?

16:56.266 --> 16:59.133
When you die, everything ends.

16:59.235 --> 17:01.328
Can you do such a thing?

17:01.437 --> 17:04.497
It's better than
dying of boredom at your place.

17:05.575 --> 17:06.940
You shouldn't, Satsuki.

17:13.183 --> 17:14.150
Yuto...

17:17.587 --> 17:20.215
This time,
it's your turn to choose.

17:20.323 --> 17:21.950
Do you want to die now...

17:22.058 --> 17:25.027
...or swear you'll never
get close to Satsuki?

17:25.128 --> 17:26.186
Damn you.

17:26.296 --> 17:27.854
You won't get away with this.

17:27.964 --> 17:30.262
You're going to let me
get away with it.

17:30.366 --> 17:32.163
Now, which will it be?

17:33.603 --> 17:34.661
All right.

17:43.947 --> 17:45.244
Well...

17:45.348 --> 17:47.316
...let's go back, Satsuki.

17:48.851 --> 17:50.614
How'd you know I was here?

17:50.720 --> 17:54.554
Well, I've been out of shape,
and I wanted to exercise a bit.

17:55.658 --> 17:59.458
Oh, right. Kanoe's been waiting
for your report, Satsuki.

18:01.297 --> 18:03.197
I see, so that's why.

18:03.299 --> 18:05.995
Then there's nothing
more to worry about.

18:06.102 --> 18:10.129
I think they aren't stupid enough
to make a bigger fuss of this.

18:11.241 --> 18:13.141
And what's this about a report?

18:13.243 --> 18:15.074
Did you find something out?

18:15.178 --> 18:16.543
Yes.

18:16.646 --> 18:21.140
We entered Tojo Pharmaceuticals'
computer program yesterday.

18:21.251 --> 18:23.219
Tojo Pharmaceuticals?

18:23.319 --> 18:26.049
It's one of the biggest
in the country's industry.

18:26.155 --> 18:28.953
A strange project
is being researched there.

18:29.058 --> 18:30.650
And for 20 years now.

18:32.495 --> 18:34.520
Is this a clone?

18:34.631 --> 18:35.723
Yes.

18:35.832 --> 18:37.561
They've named him "Nataku."

18:38.568 --> 18:39.535
Furthermore...

18:42.605 --> 18:44.072
This is...

18:44.173 --> 18:48.701
...the reactions as an organism
are the same as that of a human.

18:48.811 --> 18:49.709
But...

18:53.516 --> 18:54.983
The Divine Sword?

18:55.084 --> 18:56.517
Impossible.

18:56.619 --> 18:59.452
Miss Kanoe,
what does this mean?

18:59.555 --> 19:01.955
This is Kamui's
stolen Divine Sword.

19:02.058 --> 19:04.526
The one that took it
from Togakushi Shrine...

19:04.627 --> 19:06.788
...might well be
this cloned human.

19:07.897 --> 19:09.387
That means...

19:09.499 --> 19:13.697
...that this clone named Nataku
is one of us Seven Angels?

19:15.271 --> 19:17.205
Beast's conclusion says so.

19:18.908 --> 19:20.273
This is amusing...

19:20.376 --> 19:22.139
Yuto and Satsuki,

19:22.245 --> 19:23.644
and that clone.

19:24.747 --> 19:27.614
Now I have gathered
three of the Seven Angels.

19:28.718 --> 19:32.176
I wonder what kind of people
the other four are?

19:32.288 --> 19:33.380
Well?

19:33.489 --> 19:36.583
Has your boredom gone away
even a little bit?

19:36.693 --> 19:38.354
Not yet.

19:39.696 --> 19:41.596
- However...
- However?

19:41.698 --> 19:44.531
Beast told me...

19:44.634 --> 19:46.932
...that this world was
going to change now.

19:47.036 --> 19:48.936
Yes.

19:49.038 --> 19:52.735
Satsuki, you never
ask what I long for...

19:52.842 --> 19:55.402
what I'm seeking.

19:55.511 --> 19:57.376
You never ask me anything.

19:57.480 --> 19:59.573
I'm not interested.

19:59.682 --> 20:01.513
That's what I love about you...

20:02.585 --> 20:04.416
...my cute, little Satsuki.

20:05.955 --> 20:08.446
I like talking to Kanoe
since it's so simple.

20:08.558 --> 20:11.118
She never forces
anything out of me.

20:12.195 --> 20:14.356
She doesn't expect anything.

20:14.464 --> 20:16.398
She talks as if she mocks me,

20:16.499 --> 20:19.491
but it's not as if
she's obsessed with me.

20:19.602 --> 20:22.127
She's looking at something
other than me.

20:23.740 --> 20:24.729
I once heard...

20:24.841 --> 20:29.471
...of her elder sister Hinoto,
and it might have to do with that.

20:29.579 --> 20:31.911
But it doesn't matter.

20:32.014 --> 20:34.141
It has nothing to do with me.

20:35.885 --> 20:37.648
Lately, it's strange,

20:37.754 --> 20:39.984
but something in my heart
is racing.

20:41.691 --> 20:44.683
Perhaps it's a premonition
of what's to come.
